  "diagnostic_findings": [
    "The preserved-field replay is conservative at item level: it produces no false-positive item-level classifications but misses three of four human item-level units.",
    "All seven human search_or_index units are missed in the compact replay, showing that thematic-result and search-list surfaces need stronger deterministic signals than the current preserved URL/title rules provide.",
    "blocked_by_robots is currently mapped to restricted_or_unavailable, while human review showed that collection policy and observable surface role are independent dimensions.",
    "A configured root_url with a non-root path can cause an institution-facing homepage to be typed as institutional_landing_page even when the human-observed role is homepage.",
    "Archive vocabulary can dominate pages that humans interpret as search/index or editorial surfaces.",
    "News vocabulary such as presse can dominate an institutional thematic landing page and should not by itself determine editorial role."
  ]
